Tue Oct 20 14:23:26 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Remove leftover cramfs-tools-obey-cflags.patch, no longer
  referenced since 2.2 dropped it from the spec.
- CVE-2026-8274: cramfsck path traversal via crafted dirent names,
  already fixed in 2.2 (boo#1264703)
- Spec cleanup: drop obsolete Group tag, use pkgconfig(zlib),
  and add missing gcc/make BuildRequires.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Apr 23 06:43:40 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 2.2
  * README: correct stale claims, document cramfsck, list mkcramfs
    options.
  * cramfsck: reject directory entries that extend past their
    parent's size.
  * cramfsck: check I/O return values and zero the window buffer
    in romfs_read.
  * cramfsck: fix outbuffer NUL termination and one-byte overflow
    in do_symlink
  * cramfsck: use O_EXCL when creating regular files during
    extraction.
  * cramfsck: reject dirent names containing path separators or
    traversal components.
  * Add mention of a known cramfs obfuscation to the README file.
  * Makefile: Obey CFLAGS.
  * updating to mask errors into reported value.
  * adjusting return code for errors in continue mode.
  * fixing bail-outs for non-root users in diag mode.
  * fix a printf warning.
  * undef any existing PAGE_SIZE.
- Drop patch:
  * cramfs-tools-obey-cflags.patch (upstreamed)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
